    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0326" n="194" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> J. C. S. Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 171 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Joint Chiefs of Staff to the Commanding General,
                        United States Military Mission in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Deane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-27">27 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">War</hi> 23447. TopSec to Deane from the Joint
                    Chiefs of Staff.</p>
                <p>With regard to U. S.–Russian military conversations at the forthcoming
                    conference, the United States Chiefs of Staff will be prepared <pb facs="0327"
                        n="195" xml:id="pg195"/> to exchange with the Russians estimates of the
                    Japanese situation and to discuss plans for the conduct of the war against
                    Japan, with a view to effecting necessary coordination. They will be glad to
                    discuss other appropriate subjects desired by the Russians. You should request
                    the Soviet General Staff to advise the United States Chiefs of Staff in the near
                    future as to additional subjects they may desire to discuss.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
